                    <chunk name="param_input" index="14">
                      <items count="7">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Make the faces other than the inlet OPEN instead of pinning every face to the log-law velocity: side and top faces become free-slip (zero normal velocity; the tangential velocity and the density are the interior's next to the face) and outflow faces a pressure outlet (velocity from the interior, density 1) — the symmetry and outflow conditions AIJ and COST 732 prescribe. Upstream FluidX3D has neither, so the setup refreshes the face cells from the interior every 16 steps. On by default (AIJ Case A: no worse, the synthetic arm slightly better; stable and mass-conserving on axis and oblique wind). Off = the legacy imposed faces.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">5c2f836d-af6d-44fe-bcd1-49f38316b15f</item>
                        <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Open Faces</item>
