                        <chunk name="InputParam" index="19">
                          <items count="9">
                            <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">How hard the LoD 2.x plane search is on a steep roof plane that sweeps through walls and lower roofs. Strict drops a plane left with no face and makes flat blocks of the points no plane explains; Standard keeps every plane. Auto (default) picks by the point cloud's programme, read from LiDAR Site's LAS: Strict for swissSURFACE3D, where it removed the sails and slots on every count (Zurich, 2026-11-01), Standard elsewhere, where it did not. The banner says 'strict roofs' when that is what ran.</item>
                            <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">e1273445-5c68-4078-b9ce-edde6f7d90ea</item>
                            <item name="Multiple" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                            <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Roof Fit</item>
                            <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Fit</item>
                            <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                            <item name="Options" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Auto
Standard
Strict</item>
                            <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                            <item name="Value" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Auto</item>
                          </items>
